{noformat}public getTipsAvailability = async (ctx: Context, orderId: number): Promise<TipAvailability> => {
    const data = await this.priceNegotiationTable.loadPriceNegotiationStatus(ctx, orderId);
    if (!data) {
        logger.error(ctx, "Could not find price negotiation row for order", {orderId});
        return {isAvailable: false, isExpired: true};
    }

    return {
        isAvailable: data.negotiation_state === PriceNegotiationState.TIPPING_READY && !data.expired,
        isExpired: data.expired
    };
};{noformat}

Hello Julia,

Please find below my answers:

* are we allowed to do campaigns and pure advertising in your market? 

{color:#bf2600}Yes.{color}

{color:#bf2600}For context, in Spain there are two types of drivers: i) independent drivers and ii) fleet drivers.{color}

{color:#bf2600}The independent drivers are self-employed drivers who provide the transportation services with their own vehicles and administrative license through the Bolt app. {color}

{color:#bf2600}Fleet drivers are employees of a company (a fleet). This company  provides transportation services through the Bolt app hiring drivers for this purpose. This company that holds the administrative license and owns the vehicles is the one that maintains a commercial relationship with Bolt.{color}

{color:#bf2600}When it comes to fleet relations, apart from our General Fleet Conditions, we normally enter into special conditions with fleet companies. These special conditions specify, among other things, the percentage of the Bolt fee and sometimes include a marketing services addendum whereby the fleet partner commits to brand certain vehicles and meet certain KPIs in return for which Bolt returns to the fleet partner a percentage of the Bolt fee.{color}

{color:#bf2600}Both campaigns and pure advertising are allowed in ES and these marketing services can be provided by both fleets and independent drivers. However, it is important to assess the risks of reclassification/employee lending that this may entail:{color}

{color:#bf2600}As for the independent drivers, Labour Courts consider that individuals entering into a relationship with digital platforms for providing transport  services with their own vehicles and administrative licenses, in principle, must not be considered employees but self employed workers. Therefore, in principle, t{color}{color:#bf2600}*here are no reclassification risks when it comes to independent drivers.*{color}

{color:#bf2600}However, when it comes to fleets,{color}{color:#bf2600} *in order to avoid an illegal assignment of employees*{color}{color:#bf2600} (Article 43 of the Workers' Statute), marketing services must be provided by the fleet but not by its drivers, which means that KPIs (i.e. acceptance rate, online hours) can be linked to specific cars but not to specific drivers and all obligations arising from the marketing contract must be borne by the fleets.{color}

* if we are allowed to do campaigns, are there any specific limitations / requirements that we should take into account? 

{color:#bf2600}No. However, when it comes to fleets, it is advisable that KPIs are linked to vehicles and not to a specific drivers to avoid risks of illegal assignment of workers.{color}

* if we are allowed to do pure advertising, are there any specific limitations / requirements that we should take into account? 

{color:#bf2600}No.{color}

