Hi Team,

please see input from privacy perspective below:

* using contractor’s image for marketing/promotional purposes requires securing appropriate legal basis. Usually for this type of collaboration we use this template of authorisation and privacy notice: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1G_aZ0zWEJB-AVhy8HJ7MGdO_USTm-4Hfs28etPcPiGo/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1G_aZ0zWEJB-AVhy8HJ7MGdO_USTm-4Hfs28etPcPiGo/edit|smart-link] , it can also be incorporated to the agreement if needed;
* filming the crowd/by-standers- if the recording will be also capturing by-standers, then the area should be marked e.g. with visible stickers with an image of a camera, so it would be clear that this is taking place;
* if the by-standers/crowd would be captured in the final clip, then:
** for the close-ups, individuals who could be easily identified- we’d need a consent to legally use their image for marketing purposes - [~accountid:6131fd9fdae0a20071ad22a3] , [~accountid:638713ed9e48f2b9a614eadd] , could you please let me know if that will be the case here?;
** for the images of the crowd where no one can be easily identified - no consent would be needed, but the area where the recording will take place should still be appropriately marked.

BR,

Adriana

