{quote}We want to make this process smooth for an engineer who replicates data. Now it is based on GH PRs, and the point is that there are many mistakes / manual errors now, so there must be many commits before the change gets into prod.{quote}

With the current process I’m not surprised that there are many mistakes / errors since you’re allowed to write anything you want, there is no validation if a column or database exists, the source type matches the destination type, etc. 

By having an UI you could fetch the info about tables / columns / types from the [.sql files|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/bdc30aa757801182f55bc4830909469ba8aad62e/src/delivery/order/delivery_order_timeout/db/taxify_delivery_order_timeout.t5.db.sql#L10] in the server repo and ask the user which tables / columns he wants to replicate. For example, there could be a dropdown to select source schema, another to select the table and a third one to select columns. In this way you’ll basically eliminate any possible inconsistencies between names and types. When you submit the request - a PR is generated automatically with the information provided in the form.

{noformat}~ user_data = {
~ "Tonis Markus"            = {
id              = "P9S586A"
name            = "Tonis Markus"
~ teams           = [
+ "PAQGZIH",
]{noformat}

{quote}there is no validation if a column or database exists, the source type matches the destination type, etc.{quote}

Such validations already do exist, and are required to pass before changes can be merged. You can see a case where they found issues here: [https://github.com/bolteu/change-data-capture/actions/runs/5078290607/jobs/9122612411?pr=1974|https://github.com/bolteu/change-data-capture/actions/runs/5078290607/jobs/9122612411?pr=1974]

And indeed a logical next step is to turn this workflow around and use the validation logic to generate configurations. The steps to get there are described in the design doc that Bartosz already linked earlier: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/4377379761/2023+April+-+Managing+Ingestion+Configs|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/4377379761/2023+April+-+Managing+Ingestion+Configs|smart-link].

